LOK: Impress slide objects, guides and pictures without dialogs

- .uno:SlideObjects reads the shown slide: objects in z order (kind, frame,
  placeholder role, lock, selected; comments, which 26.2 keeps as
  objects, are left out), the selection (kind, fill, outline,
  transparency, shadow, autofit, frame, rotation and its centre, locks,
  group and ungroup), snapping, and guides. .uno:SlideDesign reads the
  current view too.
- .uno:SelectObject takes Index (and Add) to mark an object by z order,
  comments not counted, as in .uno:SlideObjects; Add without Index
  unmarks all.
- .uno:CapturePoint takes Kind, X, Y to add a guide, or Index with X, Y
  or Delete to move or remove one; LOK has no snap line dialog.
- .uno:TransformDialog takes ProtectPos and ProtectSize.
- .uno:TextAutoFitToSize takes Fit (off, shrink, grow) for every marked
  object in one step, both growths set and the text kept for undo;
  the toggle acted on one object only.
- .uno:ChangePicture takes FileName and replaces the selected picture.
- Under LOK an inserted picture lands at the slide centre; the window
  area it used means nothing there.

